# Database operations

- Run from repo root. Use `bash` for `.sh` (Git Bash on Windows). One root `.env`. `APP_ENV` = `local`|`dev`|`uat`|`prod` selects Compose, container, and volume.
- `SEED_PATH` default `database/seeds/master` (path from `/app` in the container).
- Prisma: `pnpm prisma generate` | `migrate dev` | `db seed` (skip if data exists, never wipe) | `studio`. `postinstall` already runs generate.
- Schema push only via `bash scripts/db-push-safe.sh` (checks rollout approval and refuses data-loss flags); Docker migrations also gate before Prisma generation.
- Docker schema sync is blocked by default. Before approving it, verify a fresh target backup and isolated restore; set `DB_SCHEMA_BACKUP_RESTORE_VERIFIED=true`, `DB_SCHEMA_SYNC_APPROVED=true`, the exact `DB_SCHEMA_SYNC_APPROVED_ENV`, and the reviewed schema SHA-256. A changed schema hash requires a new approval.
- Seed dump: `bash scripts/dump-master-seeds.sh` snapshots current `APP_ENV` Postgres into seed JSON (`WorkItem/` by year; leftover JSON removed) then zips to `./backups`. That site's Postgres must be up.
- `bash scripts/db-manage.sh <cmd>` (or `.ps1`): status, backup, restore, verify-rollout, health, prune-backups, connect, logs, seed, reset, force-seed — all target `APP_ENV` only. Backup/restore commands require the local Node toolchain and Docker CLI.
- Never `reset` or `force-seed` on production or any database with real data. Seed skips when configured tables already have rows.
- Backup before schema change. A file that was never restored is not verified. #16 manual backups are custom archives with checksum/inventory and isolated restore evidence, stored in approved `BACKUP_DIR` with the site name in the filename. Legacy SQL backups remain under `database/backups`; do not overwrite them.
- `restore` is an isolated rehearsal, never a live overwrite. Follow `document/DATABASE_ROLLOUT.md` for staged nullable/backfilled/required validation, history preservation, retention pins and owner-approved recovery/cutover.
- Production Compose profile `backup`: atomic daily custom `pg_dump` candidates. Owner-approved defaults: `BACKUP_DIR=./database/backups/postgres_data` from repository root and `BACKUP_KEEP_DAYS=30`. Both can be overridden; validate retention as an integer in 1..3650. Daily candidates alone are not rollout evidence.
